The calibration campaign for macOS 25G83 is now two 12-slot windows at least 6 hours apart, at least 12 retained captures, a third window only on count. July's calibration is not continued: its ceiling was set with shorter sampling frames than the machine now delivers, so the equivalence check you proposed in issue 316 would not be able to tell the two apart. Reply NO to the arm notice to stop.
W1 derivation window one: 600 s settle, 12 slots at 600 s cadence, 480 s capture budgets; window 9000 s.
